		{
			"id": "113034673692911782",
			"parentId": 0,
			"url": "https://mastodon.chateaude.luxe/@dustinrue/113034673629099925",
			"author": {
				"name": "Dustin Rue",
				"url": "https://mastodon.chateaude.luxe/@dustinrue",
				"avatarUrl": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/avatars/original/missing.png"
			},
			"date": "2024-08-27T15:24:01.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> this is _easily_ solved with a caching strategy which I have mentioned a few times to people who metion this issue. You can read about it at <a href=\"https://dustinrue.com/2023/02/avoiding-stampeding-mastodons/\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">dustinrue.com/2023/02/avoiding</span><span class=\"invisible\">-stampeding-mastodons/</span></a>. It is not necessarily something only Cloudflare can solve, but can be used to inform people on how to fix the issue using any caching solution and some effort.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "113034687493206445",
			"parentId": "113034673692911782",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/113034687493206445",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2024-08-27T15:27:33.206Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.chateaude.luxe/@dustinrue\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>dustinrue</span></a></span> WordPress always needs one more thing to work like it should by default</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "113034706341285352",
			"parentId": "113034687493206445",
			"url": "https://mastodon.chateaude.luxe/@dustinrue/113034706216934115",
			"author": {
				"name": "Dustin Rue",
				"url": "https://mastodon.chateaude.luxe/@dustinrue",
				"avatarUrl": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/avatars/original/missing.png"
			},
			"date": "2024-08-27T15:32:18.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Generally speaking I disagree. Any the site that is Next.js, Drupal or any other countless number of systems that generate content on the fly and isn't a static site will fall victim to this same issue.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "113034713252954896",
			"parentId": "113034706341285352",
			"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat/113034713252954896",
			"author": {
				"name": "Zach Leatherman",
				"url": "https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/accounts/avatars/109/286/461/031/266/152/original/dc489c3746a44e00.png"
			},
			"date": "2024-08-27T15:34:06.269Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.chateaude.luxe/@dustinrue\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>dustinrue</span></a></span> the nuance I’d contribute is that (in my opinion) static sites are a better default for most web sites and dynamism should be an additive architectural layer.</p><p>Removes an entire class of problems for most folks</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "113034724270411864",
			"parentId": "113034646645690297",
			"url": "https://mas.to/@williamoconnell/113034724246666201",
			"author": {
				"name": "William O'Connell",
				"url": "https://mas.to/@williamoconnell",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/293/897/760/366/326/original/5eb264bbdee235cb.jpg"
			},
			"date": "2024-08-27T15:36:54.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> It says they're supposed to be spread over 60 seconds though. In practice probably more, since it should take some time for all the instances to pick up the post in the first place. The author says \"I'm yet to see that work for me\" but I'm unclear of that means they have evidence that it isn't happening or their site is just still crashing regardless. The lack of specific data makes it hard to draw conclusions.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
