			},
			"date": "2024-08-29T16:45:11.916Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://noc.social/@jmhobbs\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>jmhobbs</span></a></span> great insight, thank you!</p><p>As a side note I think I’ve seen some of these caching defaults play out at the serverless platform level recently: <a href=\"https://www.zachleat.com/web/serverless-cost/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://www.</span><span class=\"ellipsis\">zachleat.com/web/serverless-co</span><span class=\"invisible\">st/</span></a> Some platforms are born from use cases that are intensely personalized, not heavily cached.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		}
